    "\n",
    "It is frozen before (a_c) and redshifts as (a^{-3(1+w_f)}) afterward. For (w_f=1/2), the post-transition scaling is (a^{-9/2}).\n",
    "\n",
    "When `match_recombination_density=True`, the notebook raises today's input CDM density just enough to preserve the reference CDM density at (z_*). This mimics the CMB compensation that is important in EDE analyses."
